---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Architecture notes"
  description="V-native Veasel Code: loopback HTTP/SSE, SQLite sessions, json2 contracts, and permission-before-effect."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / ARCHITECTURE</p>
    <h1>
      V-native core.
      <br />
      <em>Versioned clients.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel is server-first. The V application owns session state, storage,
      event history, bounded workspace tools, and the provider loop. Clients —
      the SolidJS + OpenTUI terminal UI today, anything on the HTTP API tomorrow
      — stay behind that boundary.
    </p>

    <div class="compatibility-banner">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ◆
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>
          Builder · SSE · json2 — performance without fake numbers
        </strong>
        <p>
          Hot paths use <code>strings.Builder</code>, resumable events ride SSE
          with monotonic IDs, and contracts decode through <code>json2</code>.
          We publish process-startup microbenchmarks when measured — never
          invented agent-quality scores or Harbor Index claims.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="architecture-map"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Terminal client connects to the loopback API, which connects to session storage, workspace tools, and the V agent runtime"
    >
      <div class="map-node">
        <small>CLIENT</small>
        <strong>Solid + OpenTUI</strong>
        <span>TypeScript</span>
      </div>
      <div class="map-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        →
      </div>
      <div class="map-node map-core">
        <small>BOUNDARY</small>
        <strong>HTTP · SSE</strong>
        <span>127.0.0.1</span>
      </div>
      <div class="map-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        →
      </div>
      <div class="map-node">
        <small>RUNTIME</small>
        <strong>V + SQLite</strong>
        <span>sessions / events / tools</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>State change first, event alongside it</h2>
      <p>
        Session state and its creation event are written in one database
        transaction. The event stream carries monotonically increasing IDs so a
        client can reconnect from a cursor and recover what it missed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Permission before effect</h2>
      <p>
        The model can propose a bounded replacement for one text file. Veasel
        saves its diff without touching the workspace. In the normal TUI flow,
        the user opens that diff before a one-time approval can apply it;
        application verifies the reviewed file snapshot and uses an atomic
        replacement. Shell commands require a separate review of the exact
        command, workspace directory, and timeout before a one-time approval.
        Commands inherit the server user's environment. When a platform sandbox
        backend is available, approved shell wraps with Bubblewrap (Linux),
        Seatbelt (macOS), or AppContainer+Job (Windows); otherwise it falls
        through unsandboxed. The loopback API has no application token, so
        same-user processes can call approval routes. Interrupted file writes
        and shell commands are not replayed automatically.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>What stays out of marketing math</h2>
      <p>
        Feature presence is not a task-resolution score. Cross-agent latency,
        cost-per-solved-task, and Harbor Index / Terminal-Bench / SWE-bench
        leaderboards are not claimed here. See{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/benchmarks/`}>Benchmarks</a> for measured
        process-startup artifacts only.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a
      class="text-link"
      href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"
    >
      Open the implementation plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
